{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Prevention (plan-review) for incident 1c0d — DECIDED, ready to implement\n\nPost-mortem: `9097-2741-6462-424c`. Design spike + escalation resolved (see decision comment). The old \"extend project.portability\" framing is superseded: portability is the wrong lens (credential reachability is an environment fact, not a plan fact). We ship a distinct criterion.\n\n### Necessity (why this change is needed)\nIncident 1c0d escaped because a plan (bug 8fbd's config flip) introduced a fallback chain whose terminal arm degraded to an uncredentialed/unreachable provider, and no gate required the plan to state what happens when that arm fails. The gate has no criterion that forces a plan altering failure/timeout/exception/retry/fallback semantics to declare its failure-disposition contract. Reproduced in the post-mortem; the seeded 1c0d cluster (d209 regression oracle) is the concrete motivating case.\n\n### What to build\nA **project-scoped, ADVISORY, single-turn (exec: 1-TURN)** plan-review criterion `project.failure-disposition-contract`, authored in this repo's `.rebar/` overlay (NOT a packaged built-in), mirroring the `necessity` criterion (docs/plan-review-gate.md §R4) as the architectural precedent.\n\n- **Applicability (LLM is the authority, per the rubric):** applies only when the plan adds or alters failure/timeout/exception/retry/fallback/circuit-breaker semantics; otherwise PASS. Detected from plan text + declared file_impact. rebar-vocabulary hints in the rubric: INDETERMINATE, WAIT_AND_RETRY, NEEDS_INVESTIGATION, exit-11, classify_llm_failure, should_fall_back — plus generic retry/fallback/timeout terms. No separate DET detector in v1 (keeps blast radius small; matches necessity, a pure 1-TURN advisory).\n- **PASS condition:** for each affected failure arm the plan states its disposition (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) AND, when a fallback chain is present, which leg wins on fallback-failure and the disposition of the terminal arm (the exact 1c0d root cause).\n- **Posture:** `default_posture: advisory` — never blocks. Pre-ship validation = HAND-AUTHORED bounded sanity fixtures (eval spec + committed baseline), NOT a batch corpus eval (permanently rejected on cost per §R4). Auto-monitored by the standing effectiveness recorder (zero wiring); advisory→blocking promotion deferred to the field-data gate.\n- **Bug handling:** do NOT add to `registry.BUG_TIER_CRITERIA` and do NOT set `suppress_types:[\"bug\"]`. Net effect: fires on task/story/epic plans and on **escalated bugs** (non-test file_impact, like 8fbd) reviewed under the full rubric via `ticket_type=None`; the claim-time bug exemption is untouched, so it never evaluates raw second-hand claim-time bug content — only a debugger's authored fix plan.\n- **Portability:** the concept (retryable-vs-fatal disposition per arm; preserve the most-recoverable leg) is universal; the trigger vocab is rebar-specific by design (a `project.*` criterion). Being an in-process LLM criterion it has no CI-provider dependency, so it satisfies `project.portability`.\n\n### File impact\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — register the criterion (exec:1-TURN, facet, applies_at, default_posture:advisory, block_threshold).\n- reviewer rubric prompt for the criterion (path per docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md).\n- `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-failure-disposition.eval.yaml` + committed `runs/failure_disposition_sanity.json` — hand-authored sanity fixtures.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md` / `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` — document the criterion.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Criterion `project.failure-disposition-contract` registered in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` (advisory, 1-TURN) with a reviewer rubric authored per the criteria guide.\n- [ ] Rubric applicability is self-gating (PASS when the plan does not touch failure/timeout/exception/retry/fallback semantics); PASS requires a stated disposition per affected arm + the fallback-failure winner when a chain exists.\n- [ ] Hand-authored sanity eval spec + committed baseline: catches the seeded 1c0d/8fbd-shaped case, does not fire on a clean control plan.\n- [ ] Verified advisory (never blocks); auto-included by the standing effectiveness recorder.\n- [ ] Documented in the gate + criteria guides.\n- [ ] `rebar review-plan` on this task passes (full rubric; non-test file_impact)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788142675058000564,"uuid":"5494a21b-d0d1-455f-80f8-61a0917e5326"}